ce for pung + 2 fans. But currently only 1 F2 in hand.  \n- **F1/F4**: many still available (4 each), could keep for pung chance.\n\n---\n\n**Reason:**  \nBest short-term discard is **B6**, because:  \n1. It doesn\u2019t fit a likely hand shape (Half Flush needs only W+hons, All Types would need all suits, but you only have 1 B tile and no T).  \n2. Removing B6 doesn\u2019t hurt potential honors/W-based plan.  \n3. It\u2019s safe: B6 has 4 left in wall, but B6 not recently discarded by others in history\u2014but only B3/B4/B2/B5 in discards; B6 hasn\u2019t been thrown yet. Still, safer than discarding honors that could be dangerous given opponent melds include only W suits so far.  \n\nKeep F1, F2, F4 for wind pungs (possibly double wind fans), keep J2/J3 for dragon pung, keep W3 for possible W1\u2013W3/W2\u2013W4 chow (though W1 and W2 mostly used by previous player).  \n\n---\n\n**Answer:** Play B6"}
