sible. T6-T7-T8 possible if I get T6 and T7.  \n- W9: Terminal, could pair or Pung, but terminals are useful for Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point). Unshown W9:3, so possible.\n\nBut W9 is a terminal, which might be riskier to discard if others are waiting for terminals for outside hand. However, looking at discards: many terminals have been discarded (W9, T9, B9, etc.), so maybe safe.\n\nI think discard T8 is reasonable: it\u2019s a middle tile with no clear sequence potential given T9 is depleted and T7 is available but I have no T7. Also, keeping W9 and J2 might offer more scoring potential (honors/terminals).\n\nReason: I need to progress toward a winning hand. Keeping the concealed F4 Pung is crucial for points (at least Pung of Terminals or Honors worth 1 point, and maybe part of All Pungs later). Keeping two W3 offers flexibility for a pair or Pung. Discarding T8 reduces clutter and is relatively safe based on discard history (next player discarded T5, T6, T9; across player discarded T8, T1; previous player discarded T3, T4\u2014so T8 hasn\u2019t been discarded recently, but it\u2019s not extremely dangerous). I choose to discard T8.\n\nAnswer: Play T8"}
